pose of a reverse proxy like Nginx in a deployed app?", "options": ["Routing incoming requests to the right backend service and handling things like SSL termination", "Compiling frontend code", "Storing user passwords", "Running database migrations"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''idempotency key'' solve in payment APIs?", "options": ["Prevents the same operation (like a charge) from being processed twice due to retries", "Encrypts the payment amount", "Speeds up the checkout page load", "Replaces the need for authentication"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is the main tradeoff of denormalizing a database schema?", "options": ["Faster reads at the cost of data duplication and harder consistency", "Slower reads but perfect consistency always", "No tradeoff, it''s strictly better", "It only affects the frontend"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does a ''health check'' endpoint typically do in a deployed service?", "options": ["Reports whether the service is running correctly, used by load balancers/monitoring", "Deletes old log files", "Renders the homepage", "Encrypts traffic"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is ''blue-green deployment''?", "options": ["Running two identical production environments and switching traffic between them to enable zero-downtime releases", "A CSS color scheme for deployment dashboards", "Deploying only on weekends", "A database backup strategy"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What problem does caching (e.g. Redis) commonly solve?", "options": ["Reducing repeated expensive computations or DB queries by storing results temporarily", "Encrypting stored data", "Replacing the need for a database entirely", "Compiling frontend code faster"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''12-factor app'' methodology emphasize?", "options": ["Best practices for buildin