hat is ''prompt injection''?", "options": ["An attack where malicious input tries to override a model''s original instructions", "A way to speed up model responses", "A method for fine-tuning models", "A type of embedding technique"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "Why might you use ''structured output'' (e.g. forcing JSON) from an LLM?", "options": ["To make the output reliably parseable by downstream code", "To make the model faster", "To reduce API costs to zero", "To avoid needing a prompt"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is the purpose of ''system prompts'' vs ''user prompts''?", "options": ["System prompts set persistent behavior/rules for the model; user prompts are the specific request", "They are functionally identical", "System prompts are only for error messages", "User prompts override model safety rules"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is ''chunking'' in a RAG pipeline used for?", "options": ["Splitting large documents into smaller pieces for embedding and retrieval", "Compressing model weights", "Rate-limiting API calls", "Formatting the final answer as bullet points"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''agentic'' AI generally refer to?", "options": ["Systems where an AI can plan, use tools, and take multi-step actions toward a goal", "A model that only answers yes/no questions", "A model trained without any data", "A UI framework for chatbots"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is a common risk of giving an AI agent unrestricted tool access?", "options": ["It may take unintended or harmful actions if not properly constrained", "It will always run slower", "It cannot generate any text", "It will refuse every request"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''grounding'' a model''s response mean?", "options": ["Basing the response on retrieved, verifiable source data rather 