ges", "Formatting HTML"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"question": "What does ''batch processing'' mean?", "options": ["Processing a group of tasks/data together, often on a schedule, rather than one at a time", "Processing exactly one item at a time only", "A type of encryption", "A frontend rendering technique"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"question": "Why might you use environment variables in an automation script?", "options": ["To keep secrets (like API keys) out of the source code", "To make the script run slower for testing", "To style console output", "To disable logging"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"question": "What is ''idempotency'' important for in an automated retry system?", "options": ["Ensuring repeated execution of the same operation doesn''t cause unintended side effects (like duplicate charges)", "Making scripts run faster", "Reducing memory usage", "Improving UI design"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is a common strategy for handling transient failures in automation (e.g. a flaky API)?", "options": ["Retry with exponential backoff", "Immediately give up after one failure", "Ignore all errors silently", "Restart the entire server"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''rate limiting'' mean when calling an external API repeatedly in automation?", "options": ["Deliberately limiting request frequency to avoid exceeding the API provider''s allowed limits", "Making requests as fast as possible always", "Removing the need for authentication", "Caching results forever"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "Why is it risky to hardcode credentials directly in an automation script?", "options": ["They can leak if the code is shared, committed to version control, or exposed", "It makes the script run slower", "It causes syntax errors", "It disables logging automatically"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"questio