s": ["Adding more instances/machines to handle increased load", "Increasing the CPU/RAM of a single existing machine", "Reducing the number of running services", "Compressing application code"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is the purpose of a CI pipeline running tests on every push?", "options": ["Catching bugs and regressions early, before they reach production", "Making commits happen faster", "Replacing the need for code review", "Formatting code automatically only"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''blue-green deployment'' achieve?", "options": ["Near-zero-downtime releases by switching traffic between two identical environments", "A color-coded logging system", "A method for compressing container images", "A database replication strategy"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "Why is ''immutable infrastructure'' considered a best practice?", "options": ["Servers are replaced rather than modified in place, reducing configuration drift and inconsistency", "It means infrastructure can never be updated at all", "It only applies to database servers", "It removes the need for monitoring"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is the purpose of a secrets manager (e.g. Vault, AWS Secrets Manager) in a deployment pipeline?", "options": ["Securely storing and providing access to sensitive credentials instead of hardcoding them", "Storing application logs", "Managing DNS records", "Compiling source code"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What does ''observability'' mean for a production system?", "options": ["The combination of logs, metrics, and traces that let you understand what''s happening inside a system", "A UI design principle", "A type of load balancer", "A CSS accessibility feature"], "correct_index": 0, "difficulty": "hard"}, {"question": "What is the purpose of setting resource limits (CPU/memory) on containers?", "options